@set /P CN=" ------------ Type in a number corresponding to how far back the commit is, ie. the one you saved before your most recent save would be 2, the one after it 3, and so on  ------------ When you get to the file that pops up, next to the commit(s) you want to modify change 'Pick' to the command corresponding to what you want to do, then press save and close it ------------ Make sure to press save for the file (under the 'File' option on the top left of the window) before exiting either file, or else nothing will happen. ------------ Instructions next to # are not read, they are there to inform only) ------------ What commit do you want to change the name of?: "
"C:\Program Files\Git\git-bash.exe" --cd=C: -c "git rebase -i HEAD~%CN%";read